[thin] The skirt's continuous entry taper reduces its terminal section from 3 mm to 2.3 mm over the last 1.4 mm of depth. The 0.7 mm setback guides insertion into the silicone mouth. In the production pose the outside contracts as the skirt grows upward; the saved solid PETG slice has no supports. This is a local locating-cover lead-in, not a load-capacity qualification.
alternatives: A square end removes the insertion lead-in. Keeping 3 mm through the tip requires an additional inner taper or a thicker skirt. Retain the single external lead-in and straight inner surface.
file: hardware/printed-parts/zone-c/funnel-cover/funnel-cover-print.step
